---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="Privacy information for mdbase.dev and mdbase Connect."
>
  <header class="page-intro">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="page-intro__lede">How the public website and Connect services handle data.</p>
  </header>
  <article class="legal">
    <h2>Website</h2>
    <p>
      mdbase.dev is a public static documentation website. It has no account
      system or advertising trackers. The hosting provider may retain ordinary
      request logs for security and service operation.
    </p>
    <h2>Connect accounts</h2>
    <p>
      Public signup uses an email address to deliver a one-time verification
      link. Connect retains the verified address, account name, accepted terms
      and privacy-policy versions, identity-provider links you add, and
      security and audit metadata needed to operate the account. Passwords are
      stored as password hashes, not readable passwords. Abuse controls retain
      keyed digests and bounded counters for email addresses and source
      networks.
    </p>
    <p>
      Connect also retains registered devices and their public keys,
      application declarations, collection identifiers and display names,
      collection members and their roles, exact grants, tokens, audit
      metadata, and routing metadata needed to operate the service. If you use
      an encryption password for Private collections, Connect stores your
      account key locked with that password. Connect never receives the
      password or the unlocked key.
    </p>
    <p>
      Connect uses these records, never collection contents, to produce
      aggregate operator reports: how many accounts complete setup, how often
      authorization and pairing requests are approved, denied, or left
      unfinished, and which applications are connected and in use. Direct use
      on the same computer is visible only as per-account counts reported by
      the connector. Connect does not use third-party analytics. Expired tokens,
      unfinished authorization and pairing requests, and protocol usage counts
      are deleted about 13 months after they expire or were last updated.
    </p>
    <h2>Collection data</h2>
    <p>
      For a synced collection, each change is encrypted on your device before
      it is uploaded. Connect stores the encrypted changes, snapshots, and
      attachments. It can see the collection’s members, devices, and app
      grants, the number, padded sizes, and timing of changes, and connection
      metadata such as IP addresses.
    </p>
    <p>
      For a Cloud copy collection, Connect also holds the collection key and
      keeps a readable copy, which the hosted service uses to execute
      authorized mdbase operations. For these collections, the hosted service
      acts as a trusted data processor.
    </p>
    <p>
      For a Private collection, Connect holds no collection key and cannot read
      record contents, paths, field names, or attachments.
    </p>
    <p>
      For a collection with sync off, record contents and paths stay on your
      devices. Applications reach it through an encrypted relay session with
      the computer that holds it. The relay sees routing metadata, timing, and
      sizes.
    </p>
    <p>
      If an application schedules reminders, Connect stores each reminder’s
      time and a random identifier. For Private collections and collections
      with sync off, it stores no reminder content.
    </p>
    <h2>Email</h2>
    <p>
      Connect uses your verified address for account email: verification and
      other messages about your account that the service needs to send. Beta
      accounts may also receive a short welcome and setup message.
    </p>
    <p>
      Occasionally, we may email account holders about a significant change to
      mdbase Connect or a new mdbase application. These announcements are
      infrequent and include an unsubscribe link. We do not send regular
      product updates or marketing email unless you opt in, and we do not sell
      or share your address for others' marketing.
    </p>
    <h2>Application providers</h2>
    <p>
      Applications connected through mdbase receive data under the grants users
      approve. Each application provider is independently responsible for its
      own handling of authorized data. For the mdbase Reader browser extension,
      see its <a href="/apps/reader/extension/privacy/">extension privacy page</a>.
    </p>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Report a privacy or security concern through the appropriate repository
      in the <a href="https://github.com/mdbase-dev">mdbase GitHub organization</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
